WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.600
- [Instructor] We're told that
a cone-shaped grain hopper,

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:06.710
and they highlight hopper in
blue here, in case you want

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:08.860
to know its definition on the exercise.

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:10.450
It's something that would store grain,

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:12.770
and then it can kind
of fall out the bottom,

00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:17.660
has a radius of 10 meters at
the top and is 8 meters tall.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:18.640
So let's draw that.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:22.430
So it's cone-shaped, and
it has a radius at the top,

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:25.000
so the top must be where the base is.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:25.990
I guess one would think about it.

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:28.040
It must be the wider part of the cone.

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:32.400
So it looks like this,
something like that.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.470
That's what this first sentence tells us.

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:37.170
It has a radius of 10
meters, so this distance

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:42.170
right over here is 10 meters,
and the height is 8 meters.

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:45.740
They say it's 8 meters tall,

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:49.840
so this right over here is 8 meters.

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:51.640
Then they tell us it is filled up

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:54.727
to 2 meters from the top with grain.

00:00:54.727 --> 00:00:59.320
So one way to think about it,
it's filled about this high

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:03.868
with grain, so it's filled
about that high with grain,

00:01:03.868 --> 00:01:08.868
so this distance is going
to be 8 minus these 2,

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:12.319
so this is going to be 6 meters high.

00:01:12.319 --> 00:01:15.050
That's what that second sentence tells us.

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:17.750
The hopper will pour the grain
into boxes with dimensions

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:22.120
of 0.5 meters by 0.5 meters by 0.4 meters.

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:24.010
The hopper pours grain at a rate

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:26.552
of 8 cubic meters per minute.

00:01:26.552 --> 00:01:28.736
So, a lot of information there.

00:01:28.736 --> 00:01:30.830
The first question is what is the volume

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:32.659
of grain in the hopper?

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:34.570
Before we even get to
these other questions,

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:35.560
let's see if we can answer that.

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:38.360
So that's going to be this
volume right over here,

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:41.310
of the red part, the cone
made up of the grain.

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:44.120
Pause this video and try to figure it out.

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:45.510
Well, from previous videos,

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:47.840
we know that volume of
a cone is going to be

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:52.320
1/3 times the area of the
base, times the height.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:55.980
Now we know the height is
6 meters, but what we need

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:58.080
to do is figure out the area of the base.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:01:59.510
Well, how do we do that?

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:03.270
Well, we'd have to figure
out the radius of the base.

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:06.211
Let's call that r, right over here.

00:02:06.211 --> 00:02:08.310
And how do we figure that out?

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:10.770
Well, we can look at these two triangles

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:11.880
that you can see on my screen,

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:14.570
and realize that they
are similar triangles.

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:18.000
This line is parallel to that line.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.150
This is a right angle.

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:21.410
This is a right angle,
because both of these cuts

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:24.550
of these surfaces are going
to be parallel to the ground,

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:27.470
and then this angle's going
to be converted to this angle,

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:29.180
'cause you could view
this line as a transversal

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:32.150
between parallel lines, and
these are corresponding angles.

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:34.140
And then both triangles share this.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:35.580
So you have angle, angle, angle.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:36.960
These are similar triangles,

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:40.400
and so we can set up a proportion here.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.500
We can say the ratio
between r and 10 meters,

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:48.282
the ratio of r to 10, is
equal to the ratio of 6 to 8.

00:02:48.282 --> 00:02:51.410
Is equal to the ratio of 6 to 8,

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:53.420
and then we could try to solve for r.

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:58.100
R is going to be equal
to, r is equal to...

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:00.131
Multiply both sides by 10.

00:03:00.131 --> 00:03:01.850
Multiply both sides by 10,

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:05.160
and you're going to get 60 over 8.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:08.520
60 over 8, 8 goes into 60
seven times with 4 left over.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:13.520
So it's 7 4/8, or it's also 7.5,

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:15.010
and so if you want to know

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:16.790
the area of the base right over here,

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:18.690
if you wanted to know this b,

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:21.480
it would be pi times the radius squared,

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:26.480
so b in this case, is
going to be pi times 7.5,

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:28.900
we're dealing with meters squared,

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:31.670
and so the volume, to
answer the first question,

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:35.560
the volume's going to be 1/3
times the area of the base,

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:40.560
this area up here, which is
pi times 7.5 meters squared,

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:47.333
times the height, so times 6 meters.

00:03:47.333 --> 00:03:50.160
And let's see, we could
simplify this a little bit.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:53.330
6 divided by 3, or 6 times 1/3,

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:55.520
is just going to be equal to 2,

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:57.390
and so let me get my calculator.

00:03:57.390 --> 00:04:00.853
They say round to nearest
tenth of a cubic meter.

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:06.170
So we have 7.5 squared

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:12.230
times 2, times pi,

00:04:13.466 --> 00:04:18.120
is equal to, well if we
round to the nearest tenth,

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:21.823
it's gonna be 353.4 cubic meters.

00:04:21.823 --> 00:04:26.823
So the volume is approximately
353.4 cubic meters.

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:33.760
So that's the answer to the
first part right over there,

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:36.130
and then they say how many complete boxes

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:38.190
will the grain fill?

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:41.490
Well, they talk about the
boxes right over here.

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:43.430
The hopper will pour the grain into boxes

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:48.360
with dimensions of 0.5 meters
by 0.5 meters by 0.4 meters,

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:50.610
so we can imagine these boxes.

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:52.163
They look like this,

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:58.460
and they are 0.5 meters by
0.5 meters by 0.4 meters,

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:04.260
so the volume of each
box is just going to be

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:06.200
the product of these three numbers.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.190
So the volume of each box is going to be

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:11.520
the width times the
depth times the height,

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:16.520
so 0.5 meters times 0.5
meters times 0.4 meters,

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:23.990
and we should be able
to do this in our head,

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:26.720
because 5 times 5 is 25.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:31.410
25 times 4 is equal to 100,
but then we have to think

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:34.500
we have one, two, three
digits to the right

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.890
of the decimal point, so one, two, three.

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:41.057
So this is going to be a
tenth, 0.100 cubic meters,

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:45.230
so a tenth of a cubic meter.

00:05:45.230 --> 00:05:48.860
So how many tenths of
cubic meters can I fill up

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:50.763
with this much grain?

00:05:50.763 --> 00:05:53.120
Well, it's just going to be this number

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:54.687
divided by a tenth.

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:57.178
Well, if you divide by a tenth,

00:05:57.178 --> 00:06:01.027
that's the same thing
as multiplying by 10,

00:06:01.027 --> 00:06:04.000
and so if you multiply this by 10,

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:08.491
you're going to get 3,534 boxes.

00:06:08.491 --> 00:06:11.610
Now once again, let's just appreciate.

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:15.130
Every cubic meter, you can
fill 10 of these boxes,

00:06:15.130 --> 00:06:17.480
and this is how many cubic meters we have,

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:19.840
so if you multiply this by 10,

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:22.200
it tells you how many boxes you fill up,

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:23.270
and one way to think about it,

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:24.690
we've seen this in other videos,

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:27.121
we're shifting the decimal
one place over to the right

00:06:27.121 --> 00:06:31.940
to get this many boxes, and,
it's important to realize,

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:35.756
complete boxes, because
when we got to 353.4,

00:06:35.756 --> 00:06:40.756
we did round down, so
we do have that amount,

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:42.530
but we're not going to fill up another box

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:44.772
with whatever this rounding error,

00:06:44.772 --> 00:06:46.072
that we rounded down from.

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:49.810
So the last question is,
to the nearest minute,

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:52.833
how long does it take to fill the boxes?

00:06:52.833 --> 00:06:55.050
Well, this is the total volume,

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:59.330
and we're going to fill 8
cubic meters per minute,

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:03.500
so the answer over here is
going to be our total volume,

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:08.410
it's going to be 353.4 cubic meters,

00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:11.170
and we're going to
divide that by our rate,

00:07:11.170 --> 00:07:14.358
8 cubic meters per minute,

00:07:14.358 --> 00:07:19.358
and that is going to give
us 353.4 divided by 8,

00:07:21.010 --> 00:07:24.400
is equal to, and if we want to round

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:28.237
to the nearest minute, 44 minutes.

00:07:28.237 --> 00:07:32.061
Is equal to approximately 44 minutes

00:07:32.061 --> 00:07:34.623
to fill all of the boxes, and we're done.

